&lt;p style="margin-top: 11.2pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.25pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.3pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Basis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.2pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.25pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 5.15pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Mid-Atlantic Offshore Development LLC ("MAOD" or the "Company") is a limited liability company formed to develop offshore electric transmission facilities intended to interconnect offshore wind generation resources to the onshore transmission grid.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The accompanying unaudited financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting and reporting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC")&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; including the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Uniform System of Accounts (&amp;#8220;USoA") prescribed for electric utilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in 18 C.F.R. Part 101 and the reporting instructions applicable to the FERC Form No. 3-Q&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; These accounting requirements constitute a special purpose framework, or other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; comprehensive basis of accounting &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;(&amp;#8220;OCBOA&amp;#8221;), &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("U.S. GAAP").&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Accordingly, the accompanying financial statements are not intended to present the Company&amp;#8217;s financial position, results of operations, or cash flows in conformity with U.S. GAAP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 3.25pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The accompanying financial statements &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;include the accounts of the Company and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;are presented for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;June 30, 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Comparative &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;balance sheet &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;information is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;presented &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of December 31, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; Results for interim periods are not necessarily indicative of results for the full year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In the opinion of management, the accompanying financial statements include all adjustments considered necessary for a fair presentation in accordance with the FERC basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; accompanying &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;financial statements &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;have &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;not &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;been &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;audit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, review&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, or compil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; by an independent certified public accounting firm. Management is responsible for the preparation and fair presentation of these financial statements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in accordance with the FERC basis of accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 3.25pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 3.25pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Management has evaluated subsequent events through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;August 26, 2026,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;date the financial statements were available to be issued&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 3.25pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.45pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.25pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Significant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.7pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.4pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 3pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; color: #404040;"&gt;Use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.15pt; color: #404040;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; color: #404040;"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.2pt; color: #404040;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #404040;"&gt;Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 1.45pt 17.8pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Presentation of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;financial statements &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;in accordance with the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;FERC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;basis of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;accounting require&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; management to make estimates &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;and assumptions that affect reported amounts and related disclosures. A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ctual results could differ from th&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;o&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;se estimates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Estimates are revised in the period in which additional information becomes available or actual amounts are determined. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #404040;"&gt;Utility Plant and Construction Work in Progress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Utility plant is stated at original cost in accordance with the FERC Uniform System of Accounts. Before cancellation of the project, construction work in progress ("CWIP") included direct labor, materials, third-party contractor costs, allocable overhead, and allowance for funds used during construction ("AFUDC"), as applicable under FERC requirements. Preliminary surveying, environmental, engineering, permitting, and regulatory approval costs directly attributable to the project were included in CWIP.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt; color: #404040;"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;AFUDC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;represents the cost of borrowed funds used for construction purposes and a reasonable rate on other funds when so used.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;AFUDC was recorded &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;as a component of CWIP in accordance with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;FERC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Uniform Systems of Accounts and applicable FERC authorizations while project construction activities were in progress.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;For the quarter ended June 30, 2026, AFUDC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ebt of $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;145,489&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and AFUDC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;quity of $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;255,225, in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;each &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;case &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;net of any amounts written of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;were capitalized &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;before the related CWIP was &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;transferred to Account 182.2 (Unrecovered Plant and Regulatory Study Costs).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Abandoned Project Costs and Recoverability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.75pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.75pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;When a project is cancelled or abandoned, the Company evaluates project costs under the FERC Uniform System of Accounts and applicable FERC orders to determine whether the costs remain eligible for future recovery. Costs for which recovery is no longer considered probable are charged to expense. Costs for which recovery continues to be considered probable are transferred to Account 182.2, Unrecovered Plant and Regulatory Study Costs, pending FERC action. The ultimate amount and timing of recovery are subject to regulatory approval and may differ from amounts recorded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.75pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Regulated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.6pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 1.45pt 17.75pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;We account for our operations in accordance with Financial Accounting Standards Board Accounting Standards Codification Topic 980, Regulated Operations, which includes accounting principles for companies whose rates are determined by independent third-party regulators. When setting rates, regulators often make decisions, the economics of which require companies to defer costs or revenues in different periods than may be appropriate for unregulated enterprises. When this situation occurs, a regulated company defers the associated costs as regulatory assets on the balance sheet and records them as expense on the income statement as it collects revenues. Further, regulators can also impose liabilities upon a regulated company for amounts previously collected from customers and for recovery of costs that are expected to be incurred in the future as regulatory liabilities. If we were required to terminate the application of these regulatory provisions to our regulated operations, all such deferred amounts would be recognized in the income statement at that time, which could have a material impact on our financial position, results of operations and cash flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.85pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;We monitor our regulatory and competitive environment to determine whether the recovery of our regulatory assets continues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.05pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;be&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;probable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;If&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;we were&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;determine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;that&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;recovery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.35pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.25pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;these&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.05pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.05pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;no&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;longer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;probable, we would write off the assets against earnings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Management believes costs incurred and recorded as regulatory assets remain probable of recovery through future regulatory mechanisms; however, this assessment is subject to ongoing evaluation in light of recent regulatory developments described below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Regulatory Assets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Regulatory assets recorded under the FERC basis of accounting represent amounts that management expects to recover through FERC-authorized rates or other regulatory mechanisms. The Company assesses recoverability whenever regulatory developments or other events indicate that recovery may no longer be probable. If recovery is no longer considered probable, the affected balance is charged to expense in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;period that determination is made&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.45pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.7pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;had no transmission facilities in service and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;recognize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;d no&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; operating revenues during the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ending June 30, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.7pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Cash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.3pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.15pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Cash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.25pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Cash and cash equivalents consist of highly liquid investments with original maturities of three months or less at the time of purchase. Cash balances are maintained to fund ongoing development activities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.9pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.55pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is treated as a pass-through entity for federal and state income tax purposes; accordingly, the Company is not subject to income taxes at the entity level and taxable income, or loss is reportable by the Company&amp;#8217;s members. Notwithstanding its pass-through tax status, the Company is permitted, subject to regulatory approval, to include an income tax allowance in its cost of service to reflect the income taxes that would be payable by the Company&amp;#8217;s members on returns attributable to the Company&amp;#8217;s regulated activities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Consistent with accounting guidance applicable to regulated utilities, the Company accounts for income taxes on a stand-alone, regulated-entity basis as if it were a taxable corporation, to the extent of the income tax allowance reflected in rates. Accordingly, the Company records current income tax expense (or benefit) and deferred income taxes associated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;with temporary differences arising from regulated activities for which an income tax allowance is provided. Deferred income taxes are recorded as accumulated deferred income taxes (&amp;#8220;ADIT&amp;#8221;) and measured using enacted tax rates expected to apply when such temporary differences reverse.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The income tax allowance and related tax accounting are limited to taxes associated with regulated operations and do not represent taxes payable by the Company. Any differences between the tax amounts recognized for regulatory accounting purposes and the actual taxes incurred by the Company&amp;#8217;s members are reflected as differences in the members&amp;#8217; capital accounts and are not recorded as liabilities of the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.8pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company&amp;#8217;s income tax accounting is intended to comply with applicable normalization requirements, including the treatment of accelerated depreciation and related deferred taxes, to the extent such requirements are applicable to the Company&amp;#8217;s regulated operations and income tax allowance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Consistent with applicable tax regulations and regulatory precedent, normalization is not required for the tax effects associated with equity AFUDC, which are accounted for using flow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;through treatment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Fair Value of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Financial&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.65pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Instruments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The carrying amounts of cash, accounts payable, and accrued liabilities approximate fair value due to the short-term nature of these instruments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt; and Abandoned Project Costs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, utility plant consisted entirely of CWIP related to the transmission project. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;During the second quarter of 2026, regulatory actions resulted in cancellation of the Company&amp;#8217;s transmission project. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On April 22, 2026, the New Jersey Board of Public Utilities issued an order &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;in Docket No. QO20100630 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;determining that termination of the State Agreement Approach arrangement with PJM was in the best interest of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the State and authorized execution of a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;mutual &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;agreement to terminate the Amended &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;and Restated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;State Agreement Approach Agreement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; with PJM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Under the Mutual Termination Agreement, 52 out of 58 SAA Projects were cancelled or are in the process of being cancelled, including Company&amp;#8217;s transmission project. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On April 23, 2026, PJM filed with FERC a mutual agreement to terminate the Amended State Agreement Approach Agreement. On June 22, 2026, FERC approved the termination, effective April 24, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As a result, the Company has begun to wind down project construction activities and transferred from Account 107, Construction Work in Progress, to Account 182.2, Unrecovered Plant and Regulatory Study Costs, the project costs for which it intends to seek recovery under applicable FERC abandonment provisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Management determined that $949,402 of project costs was not probable of future recovery and charged that amount to Account 426.5, Other Deductions. The remaining transferred balance continues to be carried in Account 182.2 based on management&amp;#8217;s assessment that recovery remains probable. Recovery is subject to FERC review and approval, including a determination of prudence and the amounts eligible for recovery. The Company will continue to evaluate the recorded balance as the regulatory proceeding develops.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;No depreciation expense was recorded because the transmission facilities were not placed in service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 17.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0.05pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Transaction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.45pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Affiliates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 1.55pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company receives administrative, management, accounting, legal, and other support services from affiliated entities. Costs are allocated based on direct charges consistent with FERC requirements. Amounts due to affiliates are recorded as accounts payable to associated companies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Activity during the interim period is consistent with the nature of transactions disclosed in the Company&amp;#8217;s annual financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.5pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 3.15pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is treated as a pass-through entity for federal and state income tax purposes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;For regulatory accounting purposes, the Company recognizes an income tax allowance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;associated with its regulated activities and accounts for income taxes on a stand-alone basis consistent with FERC guidance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company also recognized accumulated deferred income taxes (&amp;#8220;ADIT&amp;#8221;) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;associated with property, plant, and equipment and regulatory assets and liabilities. The Company expects that such amounts will be reflected in future cost-of-service recovery mechanisms, including any approved recovery of abandoned project costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;In determining its interim tax provision, the Company reflects its estimated impact from its permanent and flow-through tax differences. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The statutory Federal tax rate is 21% for 2025 and 2024. The regulated utility earnings are also subject to tax in New Jersey, which has a state income tax rate of 9%. The&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; Company&amp;#8217;s &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;effective income tax rate for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;six&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; months ended June 30, 2026 and the twelve months ended December 31, 2025, is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;2.9%,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and 10.4%,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; respectively. Our effective tax rate differs from the federal statutory tax rate primarily due to flow-through impacts of AFUDC-Equity. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;These tax amounts are recorded for FERC accounting and ratemaking purposes and do not represent income taxes payable by the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt 17.85pt 0pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company&amp;#8217;s members, rather than the Company, are subject to examination by federal and state taxing authorities with respect to the income allocated to them, subject to the appropriate statute of limitations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Rates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.3pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.35pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.45pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Regulatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.65pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is subject to the jurisdiction of the FERC with respect to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;accounting for , and potential recovery of, costs associated with the cancelled transmission project.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company expects to recover its prudently incurred cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; under&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; FERC-authorized &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;abandonment and other applicable &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;recovery mechanisms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Any recovery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;including the amount, timing, amortization period, and any permitted return, is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;subject to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;FERC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; approval.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;As of June 30, 2026, the Company has no transmission facilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; in service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; and has recorded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; no &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;operating &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; text-indent: -17.95pt; page-break-after: avoid; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;7.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Other&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.55pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Commitments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.2pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.35pt;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt;"&gt;Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company is party to various contractual commitments related to construction, procurement, engineering, consulting, permitting, and development activities entered into in the ordinary course of business. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The project cancellation may affect the amount and timing of obligations under certain agreements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Management &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;evaluates such obligations as additional information becomes available and records amounts in accordance with the FERC basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;Management &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;believes that resolution of any existing commitments or contingencies will not have a material adverse effect on the Company&amp;#8217;s financial position.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="8" type="1"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-top: 8.05pt; margin-right: 17.85pt; margin-left: 31.2pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; padding-left: 4.75pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Subsequent Events &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;July 2, 2026, PJM noti&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;fied the Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; of pending termination of its Designated Entity Agreement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; stated to be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;effective 60 days following the notice date (August 31, 2026).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;On &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;July 7, 2026, PJM noti&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;fied&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; that the PJM Board approved cancellation of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;the Company&amp;#8217;s p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;roject and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;its &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;removal from the PJM R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;egional &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;ransmission &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;xpansion &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;P&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;lan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt; baseline upgrades.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin: 8.05pt 17.85pt 0pt 17.95pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;The Company intends to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;pursue recovery of prudently incurred &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;project &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;costs through FERC processes applicable to transmission projects that are cancelled or abandoned due to factors outside the control of the developer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;. T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;he ultimate outcome, timing, and method of recovery are subject to regulatory proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-size: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
